    "rationale": "WordPress is organized by domain-named subsystems across its whole 670k-line surface: both as folders (rest-api/, html-api/, block-supports/, sitemaps/, customize/, interactivity-api/) and as ~220 domain-named files at the root of wp-includes/ (post.php, taxonomy.php, user.php, comment.php, option.php, cron.php, rewrite.php). A centralized-routing signal also exists (49 REST controllers), but it is scoped to a single subsystem, whereas WordPress's primary request routing is wp-settings.php -> WP::main() -> WP_Query -> template-loader.php. The module signal is dominant; the REST surface is captured as a module in its own right.",
